No placeholder docs.

================================================================
151. VERSION DECISION
=====================

Inspect real release history.

Upgrade-12 creates major new customer-facing surface area.

This generally deserves at least a MINOR release if backward-compatible.

However:

do not invent releases.

Do not automatically change to 2.0.0.

Explain:

published tags
current public API
new public API
breaking changes
database migrations
CLI compatibility

Then choose SemVer.

================================================================
152. REQUIRED FINAL COMMANDS
============================

At minimum run:

python -m pytest -q -ra

python main.py --version
python main.py --help

python -m build

clean wheel install

zcoder --version

git diff --check
git status --short

Also separately execute:

PostgreSQL
RLS/cross-tenant
public API
web product
billing
customer webhooks
Python SDK
TypeScript SDK
onboarding E2E
billing E2E
release gate

If Stripe live/sandbox test exists:

report separately.

Do not require it for offline CI unless explicitly configured.

================================================================
153. DEFINITION OF DONE
=======================

Upgrade-12 is complete only when:

[ ] Upgrade-11 security guarantees remain green
[ ] SaaS onboarding persists state
[ ] organization initialization is atomic/idempotent
[ ] plans are versioned
[ ] entitlements drive features
[ ] entitlement never overrides RBAC
[ ] trial lifecycle works
[ ] provider-neutral billing boundary exists
[ ] FakeBillingProvider exists
[ ] Stripe adapter exists only if legitimately implemented
[ ] billing webhooks are signature verified
[ ] usage export is idempotent
[ ] usage cannot double-bill on replay
[ ] billing reconciliation exists
[ ] public /api/v1 contract exists
[ ] OpenAPI matches routes
[ ] pagination exists
[ ] API idempotency exists
[ ] API errors are stable
[ ] API-key scope enforcement exists
[ ] customer webhooks are signed
[ ] customer webhook replay protection exists
[ ] customer webhook SSRF defense exists
[ ] Python SDK builds/tests
[ ] TypeScript SDK builds/tests
[ ] developer portal uses actual API contract
[ ] GitHub onboarding state is secure
[ ] customer dashboard uses shared services
[ ] usage/billing UI distinguishes estimate vs finalized values
[ ] web tests are required for SaaS release
[ ] onboarding E2E passes
[ ] billing E2E passes
[ ] API/SDK E2E passes
[ ] customer webhook E2E passes
[ ] no P0 cross-tenant/product security defect remains
[ ] inherited PITR/HA/BYOK limitations remain accurately reported

